  "visual_differences": {
    "all": "The in-game Thursday dates move forward seven days to 8, 15 or 29 Sha'ban at 10:00. The native HUD uses slightly different widths, border/opacity, font metrics and square trust bar ends. The amounts, trust and countdown match.",
    "ps01, ps06, ps07, ps11": "Native label outlines, gate/marker drawing, button metrics, spacing and bar opacity differ. The walked player's white dot sits just right of the Weaver marker. The existing Make up Dhuhr control is visible. Different bar width and opacity affect the Quay marker, navigation overlap and canal-caption visibility. ps01, ps06 and ps11 show shards where the master shows thorns. ps07 shows a rope where the master shows shards. Button order, colour treatment and countdown match.",
    "ps02, ps03, ps05, ps08, ps09, ps12": "The native straight Weaver's lane view uses the existing placeholder walls, road, blue sky, and Godot materials and lighting. Panel position, borders, corner radii, opacity, type metrics and spacing differ slightly. Copy, control order and emphasis match.",
    "ps04, ps10": "The native angled Weaver's lane view uses the existing placeholder geometry and lighting. The panel is slightly shorter, letter spacing is tighter, and navigation buttons are wider. The quote, source, tone and destinations match."
